'''Nylocas Matomenos''' spawn during [[The Maiden of Sugadinti]] and [[Verzik Vitur]] encounters in the [[Theatre of Blood]].

The Nylocas Matomenos that spawn during the Maiden fight will heal her for double their remaining [[hitpoints]] if they reach her, so binding them in place using [[ice spell]]s is necessary to prevent massive amounts of hitpoints being restored.

The Nylocas Matomenos that spawn during the Verzik fight will only heal her for their remaining [[hitpoints]].

Despite never attacking the player directly, casting [[Monster Examine]] will reveal that it has a stab attack style and a max hit of 11.

Dark Lure does not work on these creatures.

==Freezing Nylocas Matomenos==

The chance of freezing (including binding and grasping) the Nylocas Matomenos during the Maiden encounter scales based on the player's magic attack bonus, with a 100% freeze rate when it is at +140. However, other factors can affect the freeze rate, such as [[Void Knight equipment]] and the [[Augury]] prayer. To effectively achieve a 100% freeze rate, the player should reach a [[Damage_per_second/Magic#Step_four:_Calculate_the_accuracy_roll|magic accuracy roll]] of (Base Magic level + 9) * 204<ref>Mikle's video demonstrates 100% accuracy on an account with far below the previously documented 22,000 accuracy bonus. The probability of catching this many freezes with a static accuracy check of 22,000 is well below 0.01%, when including further unlisted videos and testing performed.https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SdoCk5K3hZ0</ref> or higher. This threshold, at 99 Magic, is 22,032.

